// Rule: [T1105][T1053.005] Cleangulp - Localappdata Microsoft IME File
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1105, T1053.005
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents
// Purpose: Hunts for the source-observed CLEANGULP filename in the Microsoft IME-like LocalAppData directory while preserving file origin and process context for investigation.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceFileEvents for localappdata microsoft ime file using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: CLEANGULP - MicrosoftIME.exe staged under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\IME Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch Confidence: Medium Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceFileEvents Evidence boundary: a match proves only a file-system event at the...
// A match does not prove: exploitation, execution, scheduled-task persistence, C2, malware identity, or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// CLEANGULP — MicrosoftIME.exe staged under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\IME
// Classification: Hunting query — Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceFileEvents
// Evidence boundary: a match proves only a file-system event at the
// source-observed path. It does not prove exploitation, execution,
// scheduled-task persistence, C2, malware identity, or attribution.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FileName =~ "MicrosoftIME.exe"
| where FolderPath endswith @"\AppData\Local\Microsoft\IME"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType,
          FileName, FolderPath, FileSize, SHA1, MD5,
          FileOriginUrl, FileOriginReferrerUrl, FileOriginIP,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
